      "documentConcept": "CBT, mindfulness and cognitive training in PD",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:2e7c812f6f89e570b6cbcb142bd8437d24948abe6823151da191fbc99376bcc0",
      "text": "PD-adapted CBT addresses mood and anxiety through cognitive and behavioral coping skills. A randomized trial supports telephone CBT added to usual care for depression, while an anxiety trial had different results on its primary and PD-specific secondary measures. Mindfulness yoga and meditation trials suggest mood benefits in selected people with mild-to-moderate PD, but broader anxiety evidence has very low certainty. Cognitive training targets cognitive performance: selected short-term test gains coexist with negative primary and long-term trial outcomes. These studies do not establish dementia prevention. Findings depend on population, comparator, training format and outcome measure.",
